From 49d0d3e0e6c6ef0745e13bd89748316b1a763b27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:31:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generate: --vision --batch keeps one M-RoPE table region per
 slot (images share the batch)

The image position table was one per device for all batch slots (see the vision guard), so an image request had to run
alone.  Each device's table now has 1 + B regions: region 0 is the main sessions' table as before, region 1 + b
belongs to batch slot b.  Every rope kernel already reads the value a caller passes as a table row, so a slot row
passes its region's base + its cell, and no kernel changes (include/strata/program/mrope_regions.hpp).
- Slot staging: verify.cpp stage_batch (serial windows and pipelined groups), the per-row indexer append every batch
  window takes, the batch commit re-append, and the slot drafters' four position writers (mtp.cpp) add the base.
- copy_to_slot copies region 0 into the slot's region when the request has pictures or the region is not the identity,
  queued on each device before its final sync (host path and STRATA_SLOT_COPY_DIRECT), the slot marked only after.
- Regions are allocated only with --vision, --serve and --batch >= 2, after every batch clamp (~51 MiB per GPU at 262K
  and 16 slots); if they do not fit, the single table and the refusal stay.  Bases are 0 without --vision.
- INFO ... mrope_slots=1: the server sends image requests through the batch (BGENI) only then; otherwise it keeps
  running them alone.  The engine's mix refusal applies only without regions.  SYCL: --vision turns --batch off.
- Image slots stay uncached (no checkpoints, no parking, never a slot source), so image state never moves between
  slots; a follow-up turn sends its pictures again and gets a fresh region.  block_pos in text slot snapshots now holds
  base + 4b (no kernel reads it).
- STRATA_MROPE_REGION_SKIP=1: a negative control for tools/vision_batch_check.py only.

Tests (CPU): mrope_regions_test (host model: text slots while an image is read and decodes, two images, reset,
negative control), batch_rows_test staging check, serve/test_image_alone.py 17 tests incl. the handshake.  Reviewed
for call-site completeness, state/ordering and text identity.  NOT yet run on a GPU: tools/vision_batch_check.py
holds the validation (text slots and image requests equal to their solo runs, two images at once, follow-up turns,
text A/B k5 vs v1 with --vision on/off).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
